title: "KurbanChain: Hyperledger Fabric traceability system for qurban (source code and benchmark data)"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Hikmatyar
    given-names: Missi
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics Engineering, Universitas Perjuangan Tasikmalaya, Indonesia"
  - family-names: Sudiarjo
    given-names: Aso
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics Engineering, Universitas Perjuangan Tasikmalaya, Indonesia"
  - family-names: Ardigurnita
    given-names: Firgian
    affiliation: "Department of Animal Husbandry, Universitas Perjuangan Tasikmalaya, Indonesia"
abstract: >-
  KurbanChain is a permissioned-blockchain prototype on Hyperledger Fabric 2.5 that records the qurban
  (Eid al-Adha animal sacrifice) chain from the donor's wakalah contract and payment, through the
  animal's veterinary examination, share-quota assignment, slaughter within the program's time window and
  attestation by a Shariah supervisor of another organization, to meat parcels with QR labels and their
  receipt by recipients identified only by keyed hashes. The repository contains the chaincode, the web
  application, scripts for a native (Docker-free) Fabric network, Hyperledger Caliper workloads, the raw
  results of every benchmark reported in the accompanying article, and scripts that summarize the results
  and recreate the article's performance figures.
keywords:
  - blockchain
  - Hyperledger Fabric
  - qurban
  - traceability
  - design science research
  - performance evaluation
  - Hyperledger Caliper
